@startuml buy-flow-sequence
title Sequence  —  User buys a share (flow across architectural layers)

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam roundCorner 5
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

box "ui  —  Presentation" #D6EAF8
  participant ":MarketView" as UI
  participant ":GameController" as Ctrl
end box

box "application  —  Use Case" #D5F5E3
  participant ":BuyShareUseCase" as UC
end box

box "domain  —  Business Rules" #FFF9C4
  participant ":GameSession\n<<aggregate root>>" as GS
  participant ":Exchange\n<<aggregate root>>" as Ex
  participant ":TransactionFactory" as TF
  participant ":Purchase\n<<Transaction>>" as Tx
  participant ":Player" as P
end box

box "infrastructure  —  Adapter" #FFCCBC
  participant ":JsonFileGameSessionRepository\n<<implements GameSessionRepository>>" as Repo
end box

== 1. User clicks "Buy" in the UI ==
UI -> Ctrl : buy("AAPL", 10)
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> UC : execute(Request(gameId, "AAPL", 10))
activate UC

== 2. Load aggregate via the port ==
UC -> Repo : findById(gameId)
note right of UC
  Use case is typed against the
  <b>GameSessionRepository</b> interface.
  The JSON adapter is injected at startup
  by <b>AppModule</b> — the use case has
  no knowledge of files or JSON.
end note
activate Repo
Repo --> UC : Optional<GameSession>
deactivate Repo

== 3. Domain executes the business rules ==
UC -> GS : buy("AAPL", 10)
activate GS
note right of GS : <i>ensureActive()</i>  —  guard:\nsession must be ACTIVE.
GS -> Ex : buy("AAPL", 10, player)
activate Ex
Ex -> TF : createPurchase(share, week)
activate TF
TF --> Ex : Purchase
deactivate TF

Ex -> Tx : commit(player)
activate Tx
note right of Tx
  Invariant check + mutation
  happen inside the aggregate —
  no domain rule leaks to the
  application layer.
end note
Tx -> P : withdrawMoney(total)
Tx -> P : portfolio.addShare(share)
Tx -> P : transactionArchive.add(this)
Tx --> Ex
deactivate Tx
Ex --> GS
deactivate Ex
GS --> UC
deactivate GS

== 4. Persist the mutated aggregate ==
UC -> Repo : save(session)
activate Repo
note right of Repo
  Adapter serializes the aggregate
  to <i>saves/&lt;gameId&gt;.json</i>.
  Domain objects never knew this happened.
end note
Repo --> UC
deactivate Repo

UC --> Ctrl
deactivate UC
Ctrl --> UI : (view re-queries via GetPortfolioUseCase)
deactivate Ctrl

' ── Key architectural takeaways ─────────────────────────────
legend right
  | **Step** | **Architectural principle** |
  | 1   | UI knows only the **application** layer |
  | 2   | Use case depends on the **port**, not the adapter (DIP) |
  | 3   | All business rules live in the **domain** aggregate |
  | 4   | Persistence is an **infrastructure** concern — invisible to the domain |
endlegend

@enduml
